# Trivy ignore — vulnerabilities triaged as accepted, with reasons.
# Generated 2026-10-25 from the trivy 0.64.1 scan of the freshly built
# backend image (python:3.12-slim base + pinned tool binaries).
# Every entry has a re-review condition. Nothing here is silent.

# ── Class A: no fixed version in debian trixie yet ────────────────────
# The vulnerable code paths are not reachable in this container:
#   util-linux/mount/nsenter/homed CVEs need a local untrusted shell
#   in the container (none exists — no users, no setuid, non-root app);
#   libxml2/ncurses/tiff/acl are pulled by image tooling, never fed
#   attacker-controlled input by the app.
# RE-REVIEW: when the matching DSA lands in debian 13 — drop the line
# and let the gate verify the fix, do not keep the ignore.

